    {
      "id": "r20261024-a02",
      "title": "The Hidden Cost of Free Apps",
      "level": "Menengah atas",
      "min": 4,
      "body": [
        "Millions of people use free apps every day. They cost nothing to download, so why do companies spend millions making them? The answer is simple: if you are not paying for the product, you are the product.",
        "Most free apps make money in two ways. First, they show advertisements. Second, and more importantly, they collect data about you: what you like, where you go, and who your friends are. Companies then sell this information to advertisers who want to show you products you are likely to buy.",
        "This does not mean you should delete every free app. But it is wise to be careful. Check what permissions an app asks for before installing it. A flashlight app should not need your contact list. The less data you share, the safer your privacy will be."
      ],
      "gloss": {
        "download": "mengunduh",
        "advertisements": "iklan",
        "collect": "mengumpulkan",
        "likely": "kemungkinan",
        "wise": "bijaksana",
        "permissions": "izin",
        "privacy": "privasi"
      },
      "qs": [
        {
          "q": "According to the text, how do most free apps make money?",
          "opts": [
            "Advertisements and selling user data",
            "Selling phones",
            "Monthly payments from users"
          ],
          "a": 0
        },
        {
          "q": "What example shows a suspicious app permission?",
          "opts": [
            "A camera app asking to use the camera",
            "A flashlight app wanting your contact list",
            "A map app asking for your location"
          ],
          "a": 1
        },
        {
          "q": "What does the writer suggest?",
          "opts": [
            "Delete all free apps",
            "Pay for every app you use",
            "Share less data to protect your privacy"
          ],
          "a": 2
        }
      ]
